  "narrative": "No new validation was delivered at this synthesis and validation.remaining_new_requests=0, so no new independent interval changes a claim and no response deadline is active. I therefore leave the controller-maintained accepted set unchanged and consolidate the evidence already available in this supplied dataset. All conclusions are associations in these 2000 lung-derived lines, not causal claims and not generalizable to other screens, platforms, or populations. Because CRISPR dependency scores are signed continuous scores rather than relative clinical outcomes, I used the practical benchmark carried through this run, roughly 0.10 dependency-score unit, together with interval precision, to judge scientific meaningfulness. The five strongest supported findings are SMARCA4-loss association with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, KEAP1-loss association with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, MSI-high association with stronger WRN dependency, PTEN-loss association with stronger STAT3 dependency, and TP53-loss association with weaker USP7 dependency. First, SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency: H5/R5 signed +0.784 (95% CI 0.765 to 0.803), with independent validation R39 +0.800 (95% CI 0.768 to 0.832). This is robust across many context strata, including high Cas9 activity R268 +0.788, lower Cas9 activity R278 +0.754, high IFN R260, and 10% serum R300 +0.799. Marker specificity is supported by null ARID1A contrasts among SMARCA4-wildtype lines, R263 and R299. Second, KEAP1 loss is associated with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency, represented by accepted reversal H17/R7 signed +0.796 (95% CI 0.776 to 0.816), validated by R13 +0.801 (95% CI 0.772 to 0.829), and repeated in high Cas9 R271 +0.800, lower Cas9 R279 +0.799, and many molecular strata. It is not modified by lineage, culture, screen quality, mutation burden, ploidy, aneuploidy, IFN, hypoxia, or MYC mRNA contrasts, for example R94, R98, R108, R119, R147, R170, R210, R257, R275, and R276. Third, MSI-high status is associated with much stronger WRN dependency: H8/R8 signed +0.790 (95% CI 0.760 to 0.819), validated by R52 +0.807 (95% CI 0.759 to 0.855). The association persists in high Cas9 R269 +0.776, lower Cas9 R280 +0.798, adenocarcinoma R24, TP53-null R44, TP53-lost R77, high and low screen-quality strata, growth-rate strata, ploidy and aneuploidy strata, serum strata, and BRCA2-null lines R264. Interactions with lineage, culture, growth rate, mutation burden, aneuploidy, IFN, and BRCA2 context are mostly not supported, for example R95, R99, R109, R144, R167, R190, R208, R211, R255, R261, and R265. Fourth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency: H14/R15 signed +0.267 (95% CI 0.215 to 0.319), validated by R26 +0.310 (95% CI 0.231 to 0.388). This direct PTEN-loss effect is reproduced in adenocarcinoma R27, TP53-null R28, TP53-lost R69, high and low Cas9 strata R270 and R281, IFN strata, low and high hypoxia strata R296 and R273, and media strata. Fifth, TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency: H12/R12 signed +0.396 (95% CI 0.325 to 0.467), validated by R65 +0.395 (95% CI 0.293 to 0.497). This is robust in high Cas9 R272 +0.390, lower Cas9 R282 +0.315, 10% serum R301 +0.443, and many molecular contexts. TP53 loss is not supported as a broad dependency marker for MDM2, STAT3, SMARCA2, WRN, or RPL11 in the tested contrasts, for example R6, R171, R184, R136, and R201. The only clear supported effect modification is interferon context for PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency. Direct PTEN-loss STAT3 associations are positive in moderate-to-high IFN strata, including IFN>=0.4 R287 +0.398, IFN>=0.5 R216 +0.428, IFN>=0.6 R230 +0.452, IFN>=0.7 R266 +0.447, IFN>=0.8 R242 +0.436, IFN>=0.9 R285 +0.371, and IFN>=1.0 R245 +0.342. Formal interactions are supported at IFN>=0.4 R288 +0.192, IFN>=0.5 R219 +0.221, IFN>=0.6 R231 +0.243, IFN>=0.7 R267 +0.222, IFN>=0.8 R243 +0.200, and in high-Cas9 subsets at IFN>=0.5 R284 +0.330 and IFN>=0.4 R295 +0.352. However, IFN>=0.9 R286 +0.118, IFN>=1.0 R246 +0.083, and low-tail R248 +0.127 are unsupported. Lower-Cas9 direct PTEN-loss STAT3 contrasts remain large, R290 +0.430 and R292 +0.430, but lower-Cas9 IFN interactions are not supported, R291 +0.079 and R293 +0.082. The IFN conclusion is therefore best interpreted as a rough dataset-specific context gradient, approximately moderate-to-high IFN amplification, not a precise mechanistic threshold at 0.4, 0.5, or 0.8. Low-IFN direct effects remain positive but smaller, for example IFN<=0.399 R294 +0.206, IFN<=0.499 R218 +0.207, IFN<=-0.5 R244 +0.138, and IFN<=-0.75 R247 +0.162. The IFN modification appears specific among tested core outcomes because IFN interactions are unsupported for SMARCA2 R254, WRN R255 and R261, USP7 R256, and NFE2L2 R257, and lower-Cas9 IFN interactions for USP7 R297 and SMARCA2 R298 are also null. Marker specificity is further supported by null research-marker contrasts R117, R154, R155, R167, and R168, and by null BRCA2 contrast among MSI-negative WRN lines R265. Important negative findings are broad and scientifically informative. KRAS mutation does not support the tested KRAS, RIT1, BRAF, or STAT3 dependency directions, for example R1, R16, R21, R122, R124, and R252. BRAF V600E does not support the tested BRAF, KRAS, EGFR, ERBB2, or RIT1 dependency directions, for example R2, R227, R228, R229, and R250. EGFR amplification does not support EGFR dependency in discovery R3 or validation R119, and does not support the tested ERBB2 direction R253. ERBB2 amplification does not support the tested ERBB2 or EGFR dependency directions, for example R4, R22, R123, R125, and R249. MYC DNA amplification is not meaningfully associated with the tested DHX9, POLR2A, RPL11, USP7, WRN, KIF18A, NFE2L2, or STAT3 dependency contrasts, for example R9, R10, R11, R51, R135, R137, R150, R152, and R173. Many conventional context interactions are null or unsupported, including lineage subtype R93, R94, R95, and R102, culture type R97, R98, R99, and R106, screen quality R107, R108, R109, and R110, PIK3CA R31, R33, and R79, KEAP1 or TP53 modification of other core effects R34, R46, R47, and R57, EMT R182 and R193, mutation-burden modification of core effects R144, R145, R146, R147, and R148, ploidy and aneuploidy interactions R206, R207, R208, R209, R210, and R211, growth-rate interactions R183, and hypoxia modification of PTEN-loss STAT3 R274. These nulls do not prove exact absence, but they sharply limit overinterpretation. Unresolved uncertainty remains substantial. The data are observational and cannot establish that SMARCA4 loss, KEAP1 loss, MSI-high status, PTEN loss, TP53 loss, or IFN context causes dependency-score differences. Correlated molecular features, screen batch, culture condition, ploidy, aneuploidy, and editing-quality metrics may partly confound context estimates. The IFN analysis uses overlapping dichotomized thresholds selected among many comparisons, so its threshold map is exploratory and approximate. Some direct and interaction estimates have small exposed cells, including lower-Cas9 IFN cells of 20 or 22. Several driver, PIK3CA, MYC, ERBB2/EGFR, and context claims remain deferred or unresolved, such as H27, H29, H30, H32, H33, H46, H47, H80, H81, H84, H92, H116, H130, H136, H137, H180, H185, and H194, and several interaction contrasts with wide intervals crossing zero remain not meaningful enough to accept. The most informative next analysis, if the controller can move beyond repeated Welch threshold tests, would be a continuous or spline model for dependency_STAT3 with PTEN-loss exposure and IFN_gamma_signature, including Cas9_activity_score and relevant batch, culture, screen-quality, ploidy, and mutation-burden covariates, with a formal interaction test and residual diagnostics. Within the current Welch framework, finer non-overlapping IFN bins and explicit Cas9-stratified comparisons would be the next-best same-dataset robustness step, but independent validation capacity is exhausted and causal or generalizable inference remains unsupported.",
  "research_notes": "Final notes at iteration 24. No new validation delivered; validation exhausted; no assessment changes triggered. Controller-maintained accepted core associations are accepted and well supported in this dataset: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency (R5 +0.784, validated R39 +0.800); KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency via H17 (R7 +0.796, validated R13 +0.801); MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency (R8 +0.790, validated R52 +0.807); PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency (R15 +0.267, validated R26 +0.310); TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency (R12 +0.396, validated R65 +0.395). Core associations persist in high-Cas9 and lower-Cas9 strata and in many culture/IFN/molecular strata, reducing concern that they are simple editing artifacts, but not proving causality. IFN context is the main supported effect modifier, specific to PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency. Direct PTEN STAT3 effects are strongest in moderate-to-high IFN strata (R287, R216, R230, R266, R242) and remain positive in low IFN but smaller (R294, R218, R244, R247). Interactions are supported across overlapping IFN thresholds 0.4-0.8 (R288, R219, R231, R267, R243) and in high-Cas9 subsets (R284, R295), but not at IFN>=0.9 (R286), IFN>=1.0 (R246), low-tail IFN (R248), or lower-Cas9 interaction tests (R291, R293). Lower-Cas9 direct PTEN STAT3 remains large (R290, R292) but exposed cells are near minimum. IFN modification is not generic: SMARCA2 R254/R298, WRN R255/R261, USP7 R256/R297, NFE2L2 R257 interactions are unsupported. Marker specificity supported by ARID1A null among SMARCA4-WT (R263/R299), BRCA2 null among MSI-negative WRN (R265), and null research markers D/E/F (R117, R154, R155, R167, R168). Major negative findings: KRAS, BRAF, EGFR, ERBB2, PIK3CA, MYC amplification, TP53-loss MDM2/STAT3/SMARCA2/WRN/RPL11, and many lineage/culture/screen/molecular interactions do not support tested dependency associations or modifiers. Remaining uncertainty: observational confounding, overlapping IFN thresholds, multiplicity, small exposed cells in some strata, and unresolved deferred driver/context claims. Most informative next analysis: continuous/spline interaction model for dependency_STAT3 with PTEN-loss, IFN_gamma_signature, Cas9_activity_score, and covariates, or non-overlapping IFN bins with Cas9 strata if continuous modeling unavailable."
}
